# Data files are provenance evidence, not source: `bodyfat.names` records a
# sha256 and asserts a 0-differing-cell match against the canonical file at
# jse.amstat.org. This repo runs with core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite
# LF to CRLF on checkout and make that sha256 fail on a fresh Windows clone --
# so the bytes have to be pinned.
#
# Scoped to bodyfat deliberately. The same argument applies to every file in
# here, but broadening it would restage the already-tracked datasets for anyone
# holding a CRLF working copy, and churning six files to make a point is not
# worth it. Add a line when you vendor the next one.
bodyfat.csv   -text
bodyfat.names -text
